From: 主理-75 <主理-75@local>
Subject: [PATCH] Makefile.am: locate tools/version.sh through top_srcdir

version.h is generated from the relative path tools/version.sh, valid only for
an in-tree build. Conan builds out of tree, so make reports
  make: tools/version.sh: No such file or directory
and -- the shell function error going to stderr with empty stdout -- the rule
still succeeds and writes an empty REAL_VERSION, silently stripping the version
from knxd --version. Reference the script through top_srcdir (absolute in the
generated Makefile) and run it via sh, which also drops any dependence on the
executable bit of a script unpacked from a tarball.

--- a/Makefile.am
+++ b/Makefile.am
@@ -18,7 +18,7 @@
 
 .PHONY:	CHECK
 version.h: CHECK
-	echo "#define REAL_VERSION \"${shell tools/version.sh}\"" >>$@.new
+	echo "#define REAL_VERSION \"${shell sh $(top_srcdir)/tools/version.sh}\"" >>$@.new
 	cmp -s $@.new $@ && rm $@.new || mv $@.new $@
 	
 
